BLOCKING — storeRepoMove() in scripts/lib/store-commands.js violates the validate-before-mutate principle. The source registry is modified on disk (repo removed via saveRegistry()) inside the search loop BEFORE the function checks whether the repo already exists in the target store. If the repo is registered in both source and target (a conflict state that storeConflicts() would surface), the function: (1) removes it from source, (2) discovers it already exists in target, (3) returns ok: false. The caller receives a failure signal but the source was already mutated. The correct fix is to pre-load the target registry and verify no duplicate exists BEFORE the source removal loop. Example fix:

  // Step 1: validate target has no duplicate
  const targetEntry = config.stores.find(s => s.id === targetStoreId);
  const targetPath = expandPath(targetEntry.path);
  const targetReg = loadRegistry(targetPath);
  if (targetReg.repositories.some(r => Array.isArray(r.folder_names) && r.folder_names.includes(repoName))) {
    return { ok: false, reason: `Repository '${repoName}' is already registered in target store '${targetStoreId}'.` };
  }

  // Step 2: then find and remove from source...
